<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 26 September, from 46 BCE to 1983.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/46-bce">46 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,071 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julius Caesar dedicates the Temple of Venus Genetrix</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Amid the celebrations of his triumphs, Caesar dedicated a temple to Venus Genetrix, the mythical ancestress of his family, in his new forum. It proclaimed his divine lineage and unrivalled power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1087">1087 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">939 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William II of England is crowned king</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">William II, called Rufus, the third son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a>, was crowned king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. He put down rebellions by barons who favoured his elder brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-curthose">Robert Curthose</a>, and in 1096 took Normandy in pledge from Robert.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-england">William II of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1371">1371 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">655 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Ottomans destroy a Serbian army at the Battle of Maritsa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Chernomen on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maritsa">Maritsa</a> river, an Ottoman force under Lala Şahin Pasha destroyed the army of the Serbian king Vukašin and the despot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jovan-uglesa">Jovan Uglješa</a>, both of whom were killed. The defeat opened Macedonia to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maritsa">Battle of Maritsa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1423">1423 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">603 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A French army defeats the English at La Brossinière</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>, a French army defeated English forces at La Brossinière, in a battle also known as the Battle of la Gravelle.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1580">1580 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">446 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Francis Drake returns from his voyage around the world</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Golden Hind sailed into Plymouth after nearly three years, laden with Spanish treasure. Drake was the first captain to complete a circumnavigation and was knighted aboard his ship the next April.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1687">1687 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">339 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Venetian shell blows apart the Parthenon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the Venetian siege of the Acropolis, a mortar shell ignited Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">gunpowder</a> stored in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthenon">Parthenon</a>. The explosion destroyed the temple's centre and killed some 300 people.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1905">1905 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Einstein's paper on special relativity is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Annalen der Physik published Einstein's 'On the Electrodynamics of Moving Bodies', which showed that measurements of time and space depend on the observer's motion. It transformed physics.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1983">1983 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">43 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stanislav Petrov judges a Soviet missile alert a false alarm</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Duty officer Stanislav Petrov saw satellite warnings of US missile launches and reported them as a malfunction rather than an attack. He was right, and may have averted a nuclear war.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 26 September <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wolfgang-count-palatine-of-zweibrucken"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wolfgang-count-palatine-of-zweibrucken.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Wolfgang, Count Palatine of Zweibrücken</span><span class="tp">1526–1569</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-hobson"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-hobson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Hobson</span><span class="tp">1792–1842</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manmohan-singh"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Manmohan Singh</span><span class="tp">1932–2024</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 26 September <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jovan-uglesa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jovan-uglesa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jovan Uglješa</span><span class="tp">d. 1371</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/thomas-clarkson"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thomas-clarkson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Thomas Clarkson</span><span class="tp">1760–1846</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/s-w-r-d-bandaranaike"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/s-w-r-d-bandaranaike.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">S. W. R. D. Bandaranaike</span><span class="tp">1899–1959</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
